{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366359-player-coup-in-an-teng-looking-for-advice","id":1366359,"title":"Player Coup in An-Teng - Looking for advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-08T11:29:00-08:00","id":1366359,"title":"Player Coup in An-Teng - Looking for advice","content":"I generally don't plan a whole campaign when I start a new game. Instead I prefer to run some sort of starting scenario and see what momentum builds up and try to plan from that. Right now, events in my new game's first session have really put me in a spot where I figure out what's going to go down.<br /> <br /> I've started running a two player Dragon-Blooded game set in An-Teng. The players are a Tepet veteran from the campaign against the Bull of the North, who've been managing her grief by building a small enterprise by taking control of brothels and opium dens in the City of the Steel Lotus as well as dabbling in infernalism (Pact with Mara) and a Nellens bureaucrat and martial artist who's overseeing and making house investments in the region. I decided to go with an adventure seed where an Iselsi pretending to be a Cynis looking for partners in starting up opium farming which needs a convenient fire to clear the current plantations. The actual plot is for the fires to spread out of control and to frame house Cynis and possibly the PCs for the loss of revenue and collaborating with an Anathema.<br /> <br /> The plot went as planned and wildfire ravaged the district but by being careful with the paperwork (Bureaucracy 5 paying off) the players managed to keep themselves out of any incriminating evidence yet put themselves in a good position to invest in the reconstruction. Then they investigated their Cynis partner and found hints of his Iselsi allegiance as well as a drop-off of information. Using this they managed to redirect an Iselsi assassin to Satrap Ragara Soras Jor. Against the odds the attack was successful and thanks to the Tepet having an in with the satrap guards they where in a position to intervene and finish of the assassin after she had killed Soras Jor. Using the momentum they had with the shock from the attack, the Nellens accessed the Satrap office and found evidence of his involvement with the Lintha and infernalism. Using the official seals of the satrap's office he appointed himself acting satrap until a new one can be assigned and sent a missive to the Deliberative, detailing Soras Jor's misdeeds with some evidence suggesting broader involvement of the house.<br /> <br /> That's where we ended the session. Their plan is to gather local members of their houses in the city to build a power-base to support their coup and find a way to win over Commander Shuri the Scarlet of the Imperial Garrison to their side, giving this whole &quot;acting satrap&quot; thing another leg to stand on. Obviously it's an insanely volatile situation but who know, maybe they can pull it of?<br /> What I'm looking for are some thoughts on how other parties will react to these event, especially Dragon-Blooded who just happen to be in An-Teng.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":913,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/913-september","user":"september","date":". 02-08-2020, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/913-september","name":"september","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar913_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T08:48:14-08:00","id":1366565,"title":"","content":"I don't remember a lot about An-Teng offhand.<br /> <br /> But I think most people are going to be of the &quot;meet the new boss / same as the old boss&quot; type of mindset.<br /> <br /> Key people who the PCs need to cement control are going to have requirement's for their loyalty -- they're going to want to be sure the PCs are right for the job, good for the Realm, and some of them are going to want personal incentives.<br /> <br /> The PCs allies and enemies, and the allies and enemies of the old Satrap, are going to care.<br /> <br /> But other Dragon-Blooded who just happen to be there... are not going to care.<br /> <br /> The Satrap changing house from Ragara to Nellens is going to cause... friction. Expect to have to make a good case to the Foriegn Office as to why a suitable Ragara couldn't be found to be acting Satrap (the Satrap gets to pick one of their four advisors... who would be the logical choice to step into an &quot;acting Satrap&quot; role).<br /> <br /> This is all assuming the PCs can keep up the pretense of being heroes who killed the assassin just a moment too late. Any hint that they set the city on fire and sent an assassin after the Satrap and you can expect the whole city to turn on their, either overtly (with a mob on the streets with literal torches and pitch-forks) or covertly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T10:10:55-08:00","id":1367252,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366359-player-coup-in-an-teng-looking-for-advice?p=1366565#post1366565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Key people who the PCs need to cement control are going to have requirement's for their loyalty -- they're going to want to be sure the PCs are right for the job, good for the Realm, and some of them are going to want personal incentives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think a lot of this will be about swaying key powerholders. It will be really interesting to see how they try to leverage the little resources they have in the region to pull this off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1366359-player-coup-in-an-teng-looking-for-advice?p=1366565#post1366565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Satrap changing house from Ragara to Nellens is going to cause... friction. Expect to have to make a good case to the Foriegn Office as to why a suitable Ragara couldn't be found to be acting Satrap (the Satrap gets to pick one of their four advisors... who would be the logical choice to step into an &quot;acting Satrap&quot; role).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good point. The Ragara advisor is probably a logical focal point for the loyalist resistance against them.<br /> <br /> I think they made a good enough case with implicating the house in Ragara Soras Jor's misdeeds that its justified for the issue to be mired down in debate for a bit. That should let the game focus on the local politics for a while with them being a state of limbo where there is neither official recognition or condemnation for their coup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/913-september","name":"september","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar913_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T20:13:37-08:00","id":1369737,"title":"","content":"Some random thoughts on the subject.<br /> <br /> A political marriage might serve to somewhat molify the Ragara, if at least one of the PCs (preferably the acting Satrap, but not necessarily) is single, i guess. And houses with a beef against the Ragara, just Soras Jor or a vested interest in the satrapy (or some specific elements of it) could get in the way or try to makee arrangements of their own.<br /> <br /> Advisors of the dead satrap can be partly dealt with by pinning suspicions of cumplicity and such upon. Even if it doesn't neutralize them, they'll have to make an active effort to get out of it.<br /> <br /> Are there any magistrates around? They could be either potential allies or trouble depending on circunstances, as without the Empress some might look for opportunities to keep their inflluence locally through &quot;threat containment&quot; while keeping a safe distance from the Blessed Isle and the slowly brewing civil war.<br /> <br /> What happened to the Iselsi? Why was it passing itself as a Cynis instead of another house, something about the Cynis as a whole, their connections in An-Teng or just a matter of &quot;the shoe that fit at the time&quot;, so to speak? What made the PCs indirect targets to incriminate? What associates and agenda does it have and how does the PCs help or hinder them? (used it because i have no idea of the Iselsi's gender - and considering we are talking of exalted, changing appearance &amp; gender for the sake of disguise ain't out of the realm of possibility even for non-lunars)<br /> <br /> How much book material or not are you using in your version of An-Teng? 3e's core, 2e's CotD: South, 1e's Blood &amp; Salt, one or more of those?<br /> That can have some influence on scenarios, available NPCs or stuff that could serve as a springboard for making new ones to ally or antagonize as they go.<br /> <br /> Power players of all tiers - mortal, supernatural, exalted - looking out for them or sketching up some and their interests can go a long way in expanding the story as you go along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-23-2020, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T23:22:00-08:00","id":1369772,"title":"","content":"Have you ever read Frank Herbert's Dune? I'm halfway through it myself in preparation for my own DB game and it's solid. House Atreides taking over control of the, basically satrapy, of Arrakis. One of the bigger things they had to deal with is spies and assassins left by the Harkonnens, the Great House leaving the satrapy. Either in the form of people who might otherwise be required to run the satrapy, but who's loyalty make them viable Harkonnen agents, or simply people hiding out in the palace or nearby areas. Then they have to work hard to make sure that the people of Arrakis side with them, since they know an upcoming conflict is inevitable.<br /> <br /> Part of how they do that is by connecting with groups of people outside of the big cities. They also make a concerted effort to distribute positive propaganda. Another thing they do, somewhat less popular among some people, is try to root out some of the corruption that the Harkonnen had let build up. It's somewhat less popular because there are quite a few people who live on Arrakis who benefit from those corrupt practices, and they're generally powerful people.<br /> <br /> Your PCs might have to do something similar, and judge for themselves how many powerful local people they can afford to piss off, or how much of the in-built corruption they're willing to take part in for their own benefit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also what do people back home think about all of this? Do the Bursars of Barbarian Tribute have a stake in that? Does the All-Seeing Eye have a stake in this? Maybe they could find some allies in the Imperial Treasury or something. Can they expect any help from their house? If a satrapy is on the line they'll definitely be able to gather <i>something </i>from the Isle to come help them cement their position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}